<oops:OOPSResponse xmlns:oops="http://www.oeg-upm.net/oops">
<oops:Pitfall>
<oops:Code>P04</oops:Code><oops:Name>Creating unconnected ontology elements</oops:Name>
<oops:Description>Ontology elements (classes, object properties and datatype properties) are created isolated, with no relation to the rest of the ontology.	</oops:Description>
<oops:Importance>Minor</oops:Importance>
<oops:NumberAffectedElements>1</oops:NumberAffectedElements>
<oops:Affects>
<oops:AffectedElement>http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/Document</oops:AffectedElement>
</oops:Affects>
</oops:Pitfall>
<oops:Pitfall>
<oops:Code>P08</oops:Code><oops:Name>Missing annotations</oops:Name>
<oops:Description>This pitfall consists in creating an ontology element and failing to provide human readable annotations attached to it. Consequently, ontology elements lack annotation properties that label them (e.g. rdfs:label, lemon:LexicalEntry, skos:prefLabel or skos:altLabel) or that define them (e.g. rdfs:comment or dc:description). This pitfall is related to the guidelines provided in [5].	</oops:Description>
<oops:Importance>Minor</oops:Importance>
<oops:NumberAffectedElements>1</oops:NumberAffectedElements>
<oops:Affects>
<oops:AffectedElement>http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/Document</oops:AffectedElement>
</oops:Affects>
</oops:Pitfall>
<oops:Pitfall>
<oops:Code>P13</oops:Code><oops:Name>Inverse relationships not explicitly declared</oops:Name>
<oops:Description>This pitfall appears when any relationship (except for those that are defined as symmetric properties using owl:SymmetricProperty) does not have an inverse relationship (owl:inverseOf) defined within the ontology.	</oops:Description>
<oops:Importance>Minor</oops:Importance>
<oops:NumberAffectedElements>18</oops:NumberAffectedElements>
<oops:Affects>
<oops:NoInverseSuggestion>
<oops:AffectedElement>http://www.softlang.org/ontologies/tbox#hasOutputArtifact</oops:AffectedElement>
<oops:AffectedElement>http://www.softlang.org/ontologies/tbox#hasPrimaryMechanism</oops:AffectedElement>
<oops:AffectedElement>http://www.softlang.org/ontologies/tbox#hasDominantForm</oops:AffectedElement>
<oops:AffectedElement>http://www.softlang.org/ontologies/tbox#hasPrimaryComponent</oops:AffectedElement>
<oops:AffectedElement>http://www.softlang.org/ontologies/tbox#standardlySupports</oops:AffectedElement>
<oops:AffectedElement>http://www.softlang.org/ontologies/tbox#hasSupportingLanguage</oops:AffectedElement>
<oops:AffectedElement>http://www.softlang.org/ontologies/tbox#hasSupportKind</oops:AffectedElement>
<oops:AffectedElement>http://www.softlang.org/ontologies/tbox#hasApplicability</oops:AffectedElement>
<oops:AffectedElement>http://www.softlang.org/ontologies/tbox#hasComponent</oops:AffectedElement>
<oops:AffectedElement>http://www.softlang.org/ontologies/tbox#assertedForLanguage</oops:AffectedElement>
<oops:AffectedElement>http://www.softlang.org/ontologies/tbox#supports</oops:AffectedElement>
<oops:AffectedElement>http://www.softlang.org/ontologies/tbox#assertedForConcept</oops:AffectedElement>
<oops:AffectedElement>http://www.softlang.org/ontologies/tbox#hasSecondaryComponent</oops:AffectedElement>
<oops:AffectedElement>http://www.softlang.org/ontologies/tbox#resolveAfter</oops:AffectedElement>
<oops:AffectedElement>http://www.softlang.org/ontologies/tbox#hasAffectedArtifact</oops:AffectedElement>
<oops:AffectedElement>http://www.softlang.org/ontologies/tbox#nativelySupports</oops:AffectedElement>
<oops:AffectedElement>http://www.softlang.org/ontologies/tbox#hasInputArtifact</oops:AffectedElement>
<oops:AffectedElement>http://www.softlang.org/ontologies/tbox#hasSupportingTool</oops:AffectedElement>
</oops:NoInverseSuggestion>
</oops:Affects>
</oops:Pitfall>
<oops:Pitfall>
<oops:Code>P34</oops:Code><oops:Name>Untyped class</oops:Name>
<oops:Description>An ontology element is used as a class without having been explicitly declared as such using the primitives owl:Class or rdfs:Class. This pitfall is related with the common problems listed in [8].	</oops:Description>
<oops:Importance>Important</oops:Importance>
<oops:NumberAffectedElements>2</oops:NumberAffectedElements>
<oops:Affects>
<oops:AffectedElement>http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/isPrimaryTopicOf</oops:AffectedElement>
<oops:AffectedElement>http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/page</oops:AffectedElement>
</oops:Affects>
</oops:Pitfall>
<oops:Suggestion>
<oops:Name>SUGGESTION: symmetric or transitive object properties.</oops:Name>
<oops:Description>The domain and range axioms are equal for each of the following object properties. Could they be symmetric or transitive?</oops:Description>
<oops:NumberAffectedElements>9</oops:NumberAffectedElements>
<oops:Affects>
<oops:AffectedElement>http://www.softlang.org/ontologies/tbox#hasPart</oops:AffectedElement>
